# Cohort list for script/cohort-cc3.sh
#
# Copy this to `cohort.txt` in the same directory and put real addresses in it.
# `cohort.txt` is gitignored on purpose: it is a list of participants, and participants
# should not be published in a repository before they have chosen to take part. Their
# activity becomes public on chain the moment they use the product, which is the right
# mechanism for a judge to count them; a committed file is not.
#
# One EVM address per line. `#` starts a comment. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# An ADDRESS is all that is ever needed from a participant. Never a private key and
# never a seed phrase. An address is public data.
#
#   Good:  0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111   (42 characters)
#   BAD:   0x<64 hex characters>                        (66 characters: that is a
#                                                       PRIVATE KEY, delete it)
#
# The script rejects a 66-character line loudly rather than skipping it, because a
# silently dropped line looks identical to a person who never started.
#
# Do not add addresses you generated, funded and drove yourself. The purpose of this
# list is to count participants, and funding provenance is visible on the explorer.

0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111
